3. Enterprise features. The Enterprise features of the Software (sending
   security events to a SIEM, the network allowlist and country rules,
   exporting the audit logs, and workspace data-retention settings) may only
   be used while the install holds an active ChatVia.ai Enterprise or SaaS
   license key for its domain (https://chatvia.ai/license). You may not change
   the Software, by any means, to use them without one.

4. Free use limits. While an install does not hold a valid ChatVia.ai license
   key for its domain (https://chatvia.ai/license), it may not:

   a. create a workspace when it already has one;
   b. use the Software's API;
   c. use voice conversations, live chat (handing a chat from an agent to a
      person), or the built-in capabilities (charts, calendar booking, forms
      and leads, image generation, audio generation and video generation);
   d. serve an agent's hosted chat on a custom domain (a domain other than
      the install's own);
   e. change the options of how texts are split into chunks (the Splitting
      settings);
   f. read the sentiment, tone, topics and sources analytics of its
      conversations; or
   g. show a logo or favicons (the icons of browser tabs) of its own in place
      of the ChatVia.ai ones.

   You may not change the Software, by any means, to go past these limits
   without a license key.

5. Selling the Software as a service. You may not offer the Software, or a
   work based on it, to other people or companies as a hosted service (where
   they use an install that you run instead of running their own) unless that
   install holds an active ChatVia.ai SaaS license key for its domain
   (https://chatvia.ai/license). Using the Software for your own organization,
   including chats with your own customers, is not offering it as a service.

6. If you do not meet condition 2, 3, 4 or 5, the permission granted above ends
   automatically. It comes back if you restore the credit, stop using the
   Enterprise features, bring the install back within the free use limits,
   stop offering the Software as a service, or get a license key, within 30
   days after you learn of the breach.

